The given input is already in the required JSON format. Here is how you can access its contents:

```python
import json

input_str = """
{
  "output_list": [
    {
      "function_name": "feeFor",
      "code": "          {                                require(balanceOf[to] != 0);
                                    if (validAfter[to].ts + mustHoldFor < now) validAfter[to].last = balanceOf[to];
                                    else validAfter[to].last = validAfter[to].last;
                                    if (validAfter[to].last > balanceOf[to]) validAfter[to].last = balanceOf[to];
                                }",
      "vulnerability": "Initial Time",
      "reason": "Assuming the constructor calls mint(owner, mintAmount) or similar method, some addresses may mistakenly bypass the vesting restriction even after the period has passed."
    }
  ]
}
"""

data = json.loads(input_str)

for obj in data['output_list']:
    print(f"Function Name: {obj['function_name']}")
    print(f"Code: {obj['code']}")
    print(f"Vulnerability: {obj['vulnerability']}")
    print(f"Reason: {obj['reason']}")
    print()

```

This code will output the details of the function in the given JSON format. It parses the JSON string, then iterates through each item in the `output_list` array, printing out the details of each function one by one.